<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Sigismund Zápolya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1540–1571</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as John II of Hungary, John Sigismund</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Sigismund Zápolya was the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-zapolya">John Zápolya</a>, king of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isabella-jagiellon">Isabella Jagiellon</a>, elected king as an infant in 1540 under Ottoman protection. He ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alba-iulia">Gyulafehérvár</a> and supported the Diet of Torda's decree of religious freedom in 1568. By the Treaty of Speyer in 1570 he gave up the royal title and became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-of-transylvania">Prince of Transylvania</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-sigismund-zapolya.jpg" alt="John Sigismund Zápolya" width="320" height="419" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dominicus Custos · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jan_Zygmunt_Zapolya.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
